.TH QFW-SLURM-BB 8 "September 2026" "qfw-slurm 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
qfw-slurm-bb \- private QFw burst-buffer lifecycle helper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qfw-slurm-bb
.I operation
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw-slurm-bb
is the private command invoked by qfw-slurm's burst-buffer Lua provider. It
parses the internal QFW directive, delegates typed QSGP operations to
.BR qfw-slurm-driver (1),
and atomically maintains protected allocation state.
.PP
Administrators should normally configure it through
.BR qfw-slurm-burst-buffer.conf (5)
rather than invoke it directly.
.SH OPERATIONS
.TP
.B evaluate
Perform one non-binding QPM admission evaluation. Exit status 10 means Slurm
should keep the job pending and poll later.
.TP
.B reserve
Perform one final reservation after compute nodes are assigned. Accepted
state is recorded for controller retry and teardown. The gateway journal owns
the authoritative tuples. Exit status 10 means a QPM reports a delay; the Lua
provider pauses and reserves again, with the nodes assigned, until the QPM
accepts, the attempt limit is exhausted or its wait budget ends. Status 20 is
permanent rejection or attempt exhaustion. Status 30 is a transient failure,
which the Lua provider retries a bounded number of times. Whenever the
provider gives up it records the reason in the job's AdminComment and
cancels the job, because Slurm would otherwise requeue it in a state it
never schedules again. See
.BR qfw-slurm-burst-buffer.conf (5)
and
.BR qfw-slurm (7).
.TP
.B release
Attempt allocation-wide release. Missing local state does not suppress the
gateway request when the cluster identity is configured. The operation always
returns success after recording any unresolved result.
.TP
.B status
Print the protected allocation state as JSON.
.SH STATE
Controller-local JSON state is keyed by cluster and job ID. Files use atomic
replacement and mode 0600 inside a mode 0700 SlurmUser-owned directory. No
state file is consumed by compute nodes. Remote SPANK retrieves accepted tuples
from the gateway journal.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including best-effort release completion.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid request or directive.
.TP
.B 10
Delayed admission. Stage-in reports it to Slurm as busy; pre-run waits and
reserves again.
.TP
.B 20
Permanent rejection or exhausted final-reservation attempts.
.TP
.B 30
Operational, transport, state, or response failure. Pre-run retries a
reserve operation that ends this way before it cancels the job.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-slurm-driver (1),
.BR qfw-slurm-burst-buffer.conf (5),
.BR qfw-slurm (7)
